":1.65,"top1_hit_rate":1.0},{"seed":4,"silted_drains":[7382,7396,7413,7034],"wet_junctions":168,"superposition_mean_cm":0.22,"superposition_max_cm":4.0,"topk_hits_mean":2.15,"top1_hit_rate":0.95}],"recovery":{"solves":100,"reports_per_solve":10,"draws_per_scenario":20,"rule":"10 junctions drawn at random (seeded, rng 0) from street junctions whose full-model peak depth is at least 5 cm; each reports its exact full-model peak depth. Drains ranked by solved weight; the top k, k = number of truly silted drains, are compared with the truly silted drains. A drain with zero weight never counts as a hit.","topk_hit_rate":0.393,"topk_hit_rate_random":0.235,"top1_hit_rate":0.8,"all_k_found_rate":0.0,"weights_positive_mean":4.15,"weights_over_half_mean":1.59,"true_weights_over_half_mean":1.44},"twin_consistency_max_m":0.0005},"notes":["Each drain's field is the change in peak street depth when that whole drain is 70% silted, with every other drain clean, on a synthetic 80 mm storm.","The solve assumes silt effects add up. That is a linear approximation of a nonlinear model; its error against full-model runs is given in accuracy.","Recovery is an identical-twin test: silt planted in the model, reports taken from the same model. Real reports carry depth-guess error and the model has its own errors.","Delta entries under 0.1 cm are dropped. Streets are 1D channels, not a 2D grid. Canal and river backwater is not modelled.","Parameters are the calibration defaults (results/calibration.json chose defaults). Only the 17 candidate drains from the twin test are included."],"wall_s":24.2}